      "id": 190401,
      "name": "robb8888",
      "username": "robb8888",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/r/dec6dc/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2017-02-28T07:46:57.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Arcanist Lupus\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n Arcanist Lupus:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Mint. &nbsp;Not too bad. &nbsp;Both EPEs and Technological Singularities came out while the environment was being annoying. &nbsp;But I never saw the Fletchettes, which would have been nasty. &nbsp;Could have wrapped up the round before I did, but I forgot about the \"kill all devices\" rule.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Mint. &nbsp;I think I had exactly the same game as you – had to do a little scrambling to neutralize the EPEs while the environment was being annoying, and also never saw the Flechettes. &nbsp; Once Tempest had the Gene Bound Shackles, Electrical Storm, and Localized Hurricane out, it was lights out for Omni. Only an ill-fated Close Quarters Combat combined with an Adaptive Plating prevented Fanatic from delivering a 20-point coup de grace. &nbsp;Ended up with all heroes standing: &nbsp; Fanatic-7, Tempest-13, Haka-14. &nbsp;This is a remarkably effective crew for doing a BUNCH of damage in a short amount of time, with all of the extra card plays.</p>",
